WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.667 --> 00:00:22.387
Kathleen burst into tears at the sight of Jimmy as an old man.

2
00:00:22.388 --> 00:00:25.993
"Don't cry, little girl," said Jimmy.

3
00:00:25.994 --> 00:00:30.517
The children quickly realized that he didn't know them anymore.

4
00:00:30.518 --> 00:00:36.933
The middle-aged Ugly-Wugly approached Jimmy.

5
00:00:36.934 --> 00:00:39.421
The two men seemed to recognize each other.

6
00:00:39.422 --> 00:00:44.085
They started to walk away.

7
00:00:44.086 --> 00:00:49.156
"Oh no!" said Kathleen. "Where are they going?

8
00:00:49.157 --> 00:00:53.240
What will happen to Jimmy when the spell breaks?"

9
00:00:53.241 --> 00:00:57.283
"Don't worry," said Gerald. "I'll follow Jimmy.

10
00:00:57.284 --> 00:00:59.892
Clean up the Ugly-Wuglies and then go home.

11
00:00:59.893 --> 00:01:08.516
You can tell Mademoiselle that Jimmy and I are with an uncle."

12
00:01:08.517 --> 00:01:14.139
Kathleen and Mabel gathered up the pile of old clothes, hockey sticks, and brooms.

13
00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:18.430
That was all that was left of the six Ugly-Wuglies.

14
00:01:18.431 --> 00:01:24.357
"Let's hide them in the stone dinosaur," said Mabel. "He's hollow."

15
00:01:24.358 --> 00:01:29.599
"Then we can have a nice tea party with our dolls," said Kathleen.

16
00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:37.284
"That'll make us forget all about this magic."

17
00:01:37.285 --> 00:01:44.632
The girls hid everything in the belly of the dinosaur.

18
00:01:44.633 --> 00:01:47.512
Then they returned to the school for tea.

19
00:01:47.513 --> 00:01:50.949
But Kathleen couldn't forget about the magic.

20
00:01:50.950 --> 00:01:54.340
She was still worried about her brothers.

21
00:01:54.341 --> 00:01:57.522
Meanwhile Gerald got on the train.

22
00:01:57.523 --> 00:02:05.031
He followed Jimmy and the Ugly-Wugly to London.

23
00:02:05.032 --> 00:02:15.207
Then he followed them into an office building.

24
00:02:15.208 --> 00:02:21.745
On one door it said, "Mr. U. W. Ugli, Stockbroker."

25
00:02:21.746 --> 00:02:29.301
On the next floor, Gerald saw a door with Jimmy's name on it.

26
00:02:29.302 --> 00:02:31.156
He didn't know what to do.

27
00:02:31.157 --> 00:02:34.632
So he sat on the stairs.

28
00:02:34.633 --> 00:02:38.389
A messenger boy came down the steps, whistling.

29
00:02:38.390 --> 00:02:44.038
"What are you doing here?" he asked Gerald.

30
00:02:44.039 --> 00:02:46.011
"Uh . . . I'm a detective.

31
00:02:46.012 --> 00:02:49.243
What do you know about Mr. Ugli?"

32
00:02:49.244 --> 00:02:52.531
"He's awfully rich," said the boy.

33
00:02:52.532 --> 00:02:55.640
"And what about that other man upstairs?"

34
00:02:55.641 --> 00:02:59.137
"He's even richer! Those two are rivals.

35
00:02:59.138 --> 00:03:02.022
Why are you so interested in them?"

36
00:03:02.023 --> 00:03:05.710
Gerald had to think up an excuse.

37
00:03:05.711 --> 00:03:08.093
"That man upstairs is wanted by his family.

38
00:03:08.094 --> 00:03:11.032
I need to get him out of his office."

39
00:03:11.033 --> 00:03:15.002
"I think Mr. Ugli would be glad to be rid of him for a day or two.

40
00:03:15.003 --> 00:03:18.684
Go in and ask him for help."

41
00:03:18.685 --> 00:03:23.027
With that, the messenger boy left Gerald on the stairs.

42
00:03:23.028 --> 00:03:28.766
After a few minutes of thinking, Gerald came up with a plan.

43
00:03:28.767 --> 00:03:36.079
He went into Mr. Ugli's office and talked to him.

44
00:03:36.080 --> 00:03:40.777
At lunchtime Mr. Ugli and Jimmy went out to a restaurant.

45
00:03:40.778 --> 00:03:45.951
Gerald followed them and sat at a table nearby.

46
00:03:45.952 --> 00:03:49.174
The restaurant was crowded and noisy.

47
00:03:49.175 --> 00:03:53.905
But Gerald could still hear Mr. Ugli asking about the ring.

48
00:03:53.906 --> 00:03:58.828
"Oh yes, this is a family treasure," said Jimmy.

49
00:03:58.829 --> 00:04:04.020
"May I look more closely at it?" asked Mr. Ugli.

50
00:04:04.021 --> 00:04:07.927
Then he took the ring from Jimmy's finger.

51
00:04:07.928 --> 00:04:11.328
And he dropped it.

52
00:04:11.329 --> 00:04:15.545
Just as Gerald and Mr. Ugli had planned!

53
00:04:15.546 --> 00:04:18.223
Gerald pounced on the ring.

54
00:04:18.224 --> 00:04:21.877
He put it on his own finger and made a wish.

55
00:04:21.878 --> 00:04:26.359
"I wish Jimmy and I were inside the secret passage in the Temple of Flora."

56
00:04:26.360 --> 00:04:30.367
It was the first safe place he could think of.

57
00:04:30.368 --> 00:04:34.724
Gerald felt dizzy. Everything was very dark.

58
00:04:34.725 --> 00:04:38.993
How was he going to deal with Jimmy until the spell wore off?

59
00:04:38.994 --> 00:04:41.846
But there was no need to worry.

60
00:04:41.847 --> 00:04:44.035
"Gerald! Are you awake?

61
00:04:44.036 --> 00:04:46.997
I had such a strange dream."

62
00:04:46.998 --> 00:04:49.843
Jimmy had returned to normal.

63
00:04:49.844 --> 00:04:53.316
"It's that ring again," said Gerald.

64
00:04:53.317 --> 00:04:57.616
"I had to wish us here to get you out of your dream."

65
00:04:57.617 --> 00:05:00.045
"Where are we?"

66
00:05:00.046 --> 00:05:03.460
"In the passage behind the Temple of Flora."

67
00:05:03.461 --> 00:05:07.657
"But how are we going to get out?" asked Jimmy.

68
00:05:07.658 --> 00:05:12.538
"I'll wish us out, of course," said Gerald.

69
00:05:12.539 --> 00:05:16.256
So he wished but nothing happened.

70
00:05:16.257 --> 00:05:19.746
He handed the ring to Jimmy in the darkness.

71
00:05:19.747 --> 00:05:22.974
Jimmy wished and nothing happened.

72
00:05:22.975 --> 00:05:30.153
The boys were trapped.
